<!-- 13 FAQ -->
<section id="faq" aria-labelledby="h-faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Questions</span><h2 id="h-faq">Furniture inspection in India — FAQ</h2></div></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details class="rv"><summary>How much does furniture inspection cost in India?</summary><p>We publish fixed per-inspection pricing — typically 40–60% below global inspection firms for equivalent scope. A standard pre-shipment inspection is a flat fee including AQL 2.5 sampling, a photographed report within 24 hours, and a decision call with your inspector.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>How fast can you inspect a furniture order in Jodhpur?</summary><p>Same-day in Jodhpur and Jaipur, 24 hours in Delhi NCR, and 48–72 hours in Saharanpur, Moradabad and Kolkata. Every booking is confirmed within 2 hours.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>Are you a sourcing agent?</summary><p>No. Qualis is an independent, buyer-side inspection and verification firm. We are paid only by buyers and accept zero commission from factories. Our supplier shortlisting service is a fixed fee paid by you, firewalled from inspection — read our <a href="/why-independent/">Independence Charter</a>.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>What standards do you inspect furniture against?</summary><p>AQL sampling per ISO 2859-1, structural checks referencing EN 1728 and EN 12520/12521, BS 5852 awareness for UK upholstery, ISTA 3A packaging drop tests, moisture-content limits set for your destination climate, and your own product specification.</p></details>
      <details class="rv"><summary>Can you verify an Indian furniture supplier before I pay a deposit?</summary><p>Yes — and you should. Supplier verification confirms whether you're dealing with a real manufacturer or a trader, and checks export licence (IEC), GST registration, premises, machinery and export history, usually within 3 working days.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

